<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Untitled Document</title>
    <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mathjax@3/es5/tex-mml-chtml.js"></script>
    <style>
        @import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Times+New+Roman:wght@400;700&amp;display=swap');

        body {
            font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;
            margin: 0.75in;
            line-height: 1.3;
            font-size: 12pt;
        }

        .title {
            font-size: 18pt;
            font-weight: bold;
            text-align: center;
            margin-bottom: 0.3in;
            margin-top: 0.2in;
        }

        .header {
            text-align: center;
            margin-bottom: 0.2in;
        }

        .author {
            font-size: 11pt;
            margin-bottom: 0.4in;
        }

        .content {
            margin-top: 0.2in;
            text-align: justify;
        }

        p {
            margin: 0.15in 0;
            text-indent: 0.25in;
        }

        .centered {
            text-align: center;
            margin: 0.2in 0;
        }

        .placeholder {
            width: 100%;
            height: 3.5in;
            border: 1px solid #000;
            background-color: #f9f9f9;
            margin: 0.4in 0;
            display: flex;
            align-items: center;
            justify-content: center;
            font-size: 10pt;
            color: #666;
            text-align: center;
        }

        .placeholder::before {
            content: "Diagram: centered diagram";
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="header">
        <div class="title">[Title]</div>
        <div class="author">[Author Name]</div>
    </div>

    <div class="content">
        <p>[First paragraph of the document. This is the opening paragraph of the paper or article. It is the first text block that appears in the upper-left portion of the page. The text is in standard 12-point serif font with normal spacing. No column break is present yet.]</p>

        <p>[Second paragraph. Continuing the main body text. This paragraph is indented as per standard academic or professional formatting. The text flows continuously from the previous paragraph with no visual break other than the normal paragraph spacing.]</p>

        <div class="centered">
            <div class="placeholder">[Diagram: centered diagram]</div>
        </div>

        <p>[Third paragraph. This text block appears directly below the diagram in the main content area. The font size and style match the rest of the document exactly. The paragraph begins immediately after the placeholder with standard left-aligned text.]</p>

        <p>[Final paragraph. This is the concluding text of the document. It wraps to the bottom of the page and is fully justified in the original layout.]</p>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
